00:04:10,909 --> 00:04:16,909
Smaller heroes. Just as super.

2
00:08:21,818 --> 00:08:27,818
The Adventures of Sharkboy and Lavagirl is a adventure, family,
science fiction film directed by Robert Rodriguez.

3
00:12:32,727 --> 00:12:38,727
Everyone always knew that Max had a wild imagination, but no one believed that his wildest creations -- a boy
raised by watchful great white sharks and a girl with the force of a volcano -- were real.

4
00:16:43,636 --> 00:16:49,636
Now, these two pint-sized action masters will show Max that even an
ordinary kid has what it takes to be extraordinary.

5
00:20:54,545 --> 00:21:00,545
Sharkboy, played by Taylor Lautner.

6
00:25:05,454 --> 00:25:11,454
Lavagirl, played by Taylor Dooley.

7
00:29:16,363 --> 00:29:22,363
Max, played by Cayden Boyd.

8
00:33:27,272 --> 00:33:33,272
Max's Dad, played by David Arquette.

9
00:37:38,181 --> 00:37:44,181
Max's Mom, played by Kristin Davis.

10
00:41:49,090 --> 00:41:55,090
Linus / Minus, played by Jacob Davich.

11
00:46:00,000 --> 00:46:06,000
The Adventures of Sharkboy and Lavagirl (marketed as The Adventures of Sharkboy and Lavagirl in 3-D) is a 2005 American superhero adventure film, co-written
and directed by Robert Rodriguez, and starring Taylor Lautner, Taylor Dooley, Cayden Boyd, David Arquette, Kristin Davis and George Lopez.

12
00:50:10,909 --> 00:50:16,909
In the film, ten-year-old Max's dreamed-up superheroes Sharkboy and Lavagirl travel
to his world and take him to Planet Drool, where they must stop Mr.

13
00:54:21,818 --> 00:54:27,818
Electric and Minus' plan to control the planet with darkness.

14
00:58:32,727 --> 00:58:38,727
Many of the concepts and much of the story were conceived by
Rodriguez's children, most notably Racer Max.

15
01:02:43,636 --> 01:02:49,636
The film uses anaglyph 3D technology, similar to that used in
Rodriguez's Spy Kids 3-D: Game Over (2003).

16
01:06:54,545 --> 01:07:00,545
Sharkboy and Lavagirl was released in the United
States on June 10, 2005, by Miramax Films.

17
01:11:05,454 --> 01:11:11,454
It received generally negative reviews from critics and was a box office
disappointment, grossing $72 million against a budget of $50 million.

18
01:15:16,363 --> 01:15:22,363
However, it has since garnered a cult following.

19
01:19:27,272 --> 01:19:33,272
A sequel, We Can Be Heroes, was released in 2020.

20
01:23:38,181 --> 01:23:44,181
The film explores themes of imaginary friend, outcast, shark.

21
01:27:49,090 --> 01:27:55,090
The tone is thought_provoking.
